<title>UK: BAA air cargo traffic up 5.2pct Apr-Dec '96.</title>
<headline>BAA air cargo traffic up 5.2pct Apr-Dec '96.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British airports operator BAA Plc said air cargo traffic at its seven airports in the nine months to December 1996 rose to 1.12 million tonnes or up 5.2 percent from the same period 1995 with both export and import totals rising.</p>
<p>UK air cargo figures for calendar 1995 show BAA's three London airports were the largest three British airports in terms of cargo.</p>
<p>BAA traffic statistics for exports and imports, April-December 96 vs April-December 95 were as follows:</p>
<p>	 Cargo (Tonnes) Combined BAA airports exports and imports</p>
<p>			   Apr-Dec 96    Apr-Dec 95</p>
<p> London Heathrow     802,036	 795,888</p>
<p> London Gatwick	212,544	 177,211</p>
<p> London Stansted	82,723	  70,229</p>
<p> Southampton		 539	     534</p>
<p> Glasgow		   8,815	   9,178</p>
<p> Edinburgh		 5,805	   4,251</p>
<p> Aberdeen		  4,666	   4,233</p>
<p> Total		 1,117,128     1,061,524</p>
<p>	    Cargo (Tonnes) Exports ex-BAA airports</p>
<p>			   Apr-Dec 96    Apr-Dec 95</p>
<p> London Heathrow     403,141	 397,830</p>
<p> London Gatwick	103,777	  87,951</p>
<p> London Stansted	41,947	  36,075</p>
<p> Southampton		 409	     421</p>
<p> Glasgow		   4,516	   4,704</p>
<p> Edinburgh		 3,233	   2,133</p>
<p> Aberdeen		  3,024	 531,947</p>
<p> Total		   560,047	 531,947</p>
<p>	  Cargo (Tonnes) Imports into BAA airports</p>
<p>			   Apr-Dec 96    Apr-Dec 95</p>
<p> London Heathrow     398,895	 398,058</p>
<p> London Gatwick	108,767	  89,260</p>
<p> London Stansted	40,776	  34,154</p>
<p> Southampton		 130	     113</p>
<p> Glasgow		   4,299	   4,474</p>
<p> Edinburgh		 2,575	   2,118</p>
<p> Aberdeen		  1,642	   1,400</p>
<p> Total		   557,081	 529,577</p>
<p>-- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+ 5017</p>
